history and natural selection and their importance in explaining genomic patterns. The third part will introduce new data types and the challenges and opportunities with these data. We will dive into genotype likelihood and will emphasize the importance of simulation in population genetics. The course will be mostly delivered through lecturing, each interspersed with short conversations about reading assignments. Coursework involves reading literature, solving problem sets, and a course project.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: BIOMG 2800\u00a0or BIOEE 1780, BTRY 3080\u00a0or BTRY 3010, BTRY 4810, or equivalents.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Apply population genetic theory to interpret patterns of genetic data.", "Explain how mutation, recombination, gene flow, and selection affect the coalescence process.", "Develop mathematical models to describe the genetic data-generating process.", "Construct the genotype likelihood under different models.", "Choose appropriate population genetic inference tools for analyzing different types of genetic data.", "Extract and use public domain genetic data and perform sensible tests on them.", "Develop population genetic simulations with popular simulators such as SLiM and msPrime."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2867, "crseId": 360958, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "BIOCB", "catalogNbr": "6830", "titleShort": "Quantitative Genomics&Genetics", "titleLong": "Quantitative Genomics and Genetics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong":